Read-only UI source findings / precise gaps:
main.rs:3218-3220 defines pending as redraw_pending OR nonempty UI message/output queues. The capture stores only that OR, not the individual booleans or queue/source counts. Native flags are its last poll; counters can be newer.
display_link.rs:93-103 — CAMetal delegate increments callbacks, saves a Tick and marks DirtySource 4. main.rs:83-84 maps all DirtySource wakes to generic UiEvent::Wake; :3305-3313 requests redraw; :2446-2454 also requests a display frame; display_link.rs:299-305 unpauses an inactive link. A tick Wake handled after draw pauses the link can therefore rearm it without new model data. This is a source-admitted scheduling cycle / candidate, NOT proof that source 4 was the runtime producer.
main.rs:2625 discards DirtySet::drain source IDs; stop-boundary frame/callback counters and per-source wake rates are not retained. Gap: the actual source keeping pending true, and its measured interval rate, are unproven by this packet. Log says requested 75/75/75 Hz and final counts 1715, not a measured source rate.
stall.rs:497-505 replaces paused_frame with every newly encoded all-PAUSED frame; :435-450 requires latest target GPU completion plus no pending and stable counts. Recorded target 1715 vs completed 1713 illustrates the moving target, without proving it is the only cause.
load.rs:1529-1535 continues PAUSED writes nominally every 100 ms. Watched last-observed ring-head rates (using each row ring_observed_ns) min/median/max 8.884/9.828/10.657 Hz; these intervals may straddle producer stop and are NOT UI publication counts.
grids.rs:38-44 filters identical Screens; load.rs:1124-1138 only publishes a new fixture model when Grids::apply returns Some. Repeated PAUSED writes alone do not prove redraws. queue/watch_panes skip the product command lane when live_commands is None, so a permanently queued product Watch/Resize is not established here. side_loads finishes before SETTLE, so its continuing bus loop cannot simply be presumed.
Smallest proposed next proof, under a separate UI brief: deterministic tick-Wake-after-pause/rearm test and split per-source pending/wake counters. No new 967 attempt, no speculative source fix in this task.

